---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { getLegalPage, legalHref } from '../../lib/legal';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/seo';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const page = getLegalPage('external-links')!;
---

<LegalLayout
	page={page}
	intro="Links help readers go deeper. They do not transfer control or automatic endorsement."
>
	<h2>1. Links to external Catholic resources</h2>
	<p>
		Digital Catholic may link to catechetical materials, Scripture resources, liturgical references,
		historical sources, and other Catholic educational sites to help readers verify and deepen what they
		read here.
	</p>

	<h2>2. Official Church resources</h2>
	<p>
		Links to websites of the Holy See, bishops’ conferences, dioceses, religious orders, or similar bodies
		are provided for convenience and reference. Those organisations speak for themselves. A link does not
		make Digital Catholic an official channel of that body.
	</p>

	<h2>3. Third-party websites</h2>
	<p>
		The Website also links to non-Church third parties where useful for the project—for example the
		public GitHub repository at
		<a href={SITE.repoUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">{SITE.repoUrl}<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>,
		image source pages, or email compose services you choose to open from the
		<a href={withBase('/contact')}>Contact</a> page.
	</p>

	<h2>4. Independent ownership</h2>
	<p>
		External websites are owned and operated by their respective publishers. Digital Catholic does not
		control their content, availability, policies, or security practices.
	</p>

	<h2>5. No guarantee of availability or accuracy</h2>
	<p>
		External pages may move, change, or go offline without notice. We do not guarantee that linked content
		remains accurate, complete, orthodox, or appropriate. Readers should exercise discernment and prefer
		authoritative editions for doctrine and liturgy.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Links are not automatic endorsement</h2>
	<p>
		A hyperlink does not by itself mean that Digital Catholic endorses every statement, product, fundraising
		appeal, or theological opinion on the destination site. Conversely, the absence of a link does not
		imply disapproval.
	</p>

	<h2>7. Security and privacy when visiting external sites</h2>
	<p>
		When you leave Digital Catholic, the destination site may set cookies, collect personal information, or
		serve different security configurations. Review that site’s privacy notice and use caution with
		downloads, forms, and payments. See also our
		<a href={legalHref('privacy-policy')}>Privacy Policy</a>
		for practices on this Website itself.
	</p>

	<h2>8. Reporting problematic links</h2>
	<p>
		If a link is broken, misleading, or points to harmful material, please report it via
		<a href={legalHref('corrections')}>Content Corrections</a>
		or <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
